{
 "fixture": "F38-zos-definitions",
 "description": "Daily account posting on z/OS: a job whose member name (ACCTDLY) differs from its JOB name (ACCTD01), with a SET, an in-stream procedure whose defaults name a SET symbolic and that the job calls with an override of a symbolic and of a procedure step's DD, an IDCAMS step (DELETE, DEFINE CLUSTER with keys and record size, REPRO), a DFSORT step (INCLUDE, INREC, SORT, SUM) reading the procedure step's output by referback and writing a data set named through a symbolic with no value, an IKJEFT01 step (RUN PROGRAM with a plan, a REXX exec), IF/THEN/ELSE around a call of the cataloged procedure in jcl/ACCTARCH.prc (a GDG generation from a symbolic) and a program; small COBOL programs; and under .rkp/inputs/zos/ a CICS CSD export (a transaction, its program, a file, a DB2ENTRY), a DCLGEN member, BIND PACKAGE and PLAN cards, DB2 DDL in a .ddl member and a DFSORT control member. Only what the zos pack emits is asserted; RUNS and EXPOSES name the COBOL programs by the shared key (contract 11.1 item 2). 'since' names the milestone whose compiler must produce the item.",
